														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4848120">
									

<p>Idea Post:</p>
<p>Seeking Greenlights: Primarily Yes</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Genre (Optional): Horror a lot, Drama/Emotional a good deal, History a little.</p>
<p>Page Layout (Optional): Basic special containment procedures and description followed by how it was obtained, then testing logs, and finally incident reports (maybe).</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: Photobook slash journal used by a former researcher working at an asylum (the early ’50s to ’70s) studying primarily murderous and violent patients. People who place a photo in the book begin to have their memories and their personalities overwritten with psychotic patients.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: I want to highlight the malpractices and the sickening practices of asylums that studied the brains of ‘psychotic’ individuals. Reports of weird experiments have always been rumored and very few reports survive from these places because some of these acts were perpetrated by leading scientists who used this research to better our understanding of psychology. There are even reports of human sacrifices and brutal use of pagan rituals and some real dark sh. Whether or not these are real stories says what if they were really basically.</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: What is unique in my opinion are the stories the imprinted patients can tell to people, the horrors they experienced, and how it happened.</p>
<p>Additional Notes: I know there are no factual claims to the horrors of such asylums in real life but I just want to tell the story, please don’t come to tell me why it isn't factual. It's SCP it ain’t meant to be factual it's meant to be fun!</p>

							</div>

										<div class="signature">
					<hr class="signature-separator"/>
					

<p>So I didn't know what else to put here so I put a favorite quote, &quot;Who wants to become a writer? And why? Because it’s the answer to everything. … It’s the streaming reason for living. To note, to pin down, to build up, to create, to be astonished at nothing, to cherish the oddities, to let nothing go down the drain, to make something, to make a great flower out of life, even if it’s a cactus.&quot;</p>

				</div>
					
					
