			<div class="content" id="post-content-4848087">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Genre (Optional): Drama/Emotional</p>
<p>Page Layout (Optional): SCP research article with addendums about the experiments conducted.</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: An old, abandoned house in New Hampshire with a room upstairs. If you're in the room and can't reach the door it will snap shut and anyone inside disappears. At the exact same moment, four exact copies of that person or those people, linked through physical experience, are generated in four random places on the planet, with one of them in mortal peril and the rest left to experience the death as an introduction to their new, linked experience.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: the house generates people who share physical experiences, and immediately causes one of them to be placed into a situation where they will die. Some of the experiments done on the room after it's discovery had mixed results, however research would have been paused after a character that I think would be useful for other things would be the sole survivor, the three other copies dying within days of their creation. Outside of the death at the beginning, which shocks many who experience it, the three share physical experiences and can communicate in limited fashion with each other. The Foundation experiments with the SCP, first confirming it's safety as well as confirming the sanity and normality of the copies before making a small team of operators, three copies of the same agent, using the SCP after it's experimentation shows it's safe status. That status is revoked when the second person sent through, a higher level operator specializing in Keter Class wet work, becomes the 'sole survivor.' Rather than experiencing a coming together of support and love of his other copies after grieving together, creating a unit far more capable than most, the Sole Survivor experiences their death three times and has a mental breakdown, joining the Chaos.</p>
<p>I have more details/ideas written out as a draft of sorts if you want a link.</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: a house in the middle of nowhere that creates linked copies of people random places around the planet and connects their physical experiences.</p>

