														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4848061">
									

<p>Oh No! When editing I took out the lines where I explained what I meant by &quot;encourages you to act on your intrusive thoughts!&quot; So, intrusive thoughts are thoughts that you have impulsively. More often than not these thoughts are violent. People who have been affected by this &quot;magic earworm&quot; have committed acts from strange but harmless behavior all the way up to homicide and self-mutilation. This was actually inspired by something that happened to me the other day. I was cooking and chopping onions and I was singing a song in my head, when an intrusive thought popped up and said &quot;chop your finger off.&quot; I started singing &quot;chop your finger off&quot; to the tune of the song that was stuck in my head. I feel so dumb for leaving out the explanation. I was erasing fluff lines to stay under the word count but I must have erased the wrong ones.</p>
<p>Also, I'm glad you asked about if it can appear randomly. Yes it absolutely can. That is how the phenomenon starts in Patient 0, seemingly at random. The Foundation has contained at least a dozen outbreaks in the past, all in different areas around the world. Usually, these outbreaks are 5-10 years apart from each other and leads credence to the &quot;phenomenon theory.&quot; However, the past three outbreaks have all been within the past three years. The staff that believes in the &quot;entity theory &quot;believes the entity is going through a sort of molting period, they believe that this entity feeds on sanity and is about to evolve. So it requires more sustenance and is moving at a much faster rate. In the original findings, people who had the &quot;Jukebug&quot; could not transmit it through recordings, and it was safe to record any singing the afflicted did. However within the past three years, the &quot;Jukebug&quot; phenomenon or entity has evolved to be able to spread through audio and visual recording, so the Foundation has revoked clearance for recording.</p>
<p>I know it seems like a lot I left out in the pitch, however I wanted the basics explained first, which I apparently failed to do. Thank you for your input and for taking the time to read this.</p>

